  <event id="289">
      <start>10:15</start>
      <duration>00:45</duration>
      <room>H.1309</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>GUPnP &amp; Rygel: Liberating Digital Living</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>CrossDesktop</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;GUPnP is an object-oriented C library to ease the task for writing UPnP/DLNA applications. Rygel is a collection of DLNA services built on top of GUPnP in Vala language.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I will start the presentation with an introduction of both projects and how they are designed from ground-up for both desktop and mobile environments. After that I will introduce the existing and planed features. I will then introduce the plugin API of Rygel with the help of a Sample plugin, followed by a demo and Q&amp;amp;A session in the end.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;  </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="2891">Zeeshan Ali</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>